# Patch: Add copyFragment → generateUniqueFragmentTitle integration test

## Metadata
adw_id: ``
review_change_request: `Issue #1: No integration test covers the copyFragment → generateUniqueFragmentTitle call path. The helper is tested in isolation but nothing asserts that copyFragment passes the correct (requestedTitle, parentPath) arguments. Resolution: Add a test in the copyFragment describe block that stubs generateUniqueFragmentTitle and asserts it is called with the expected arguments derived from result.path and updatedTitle. Severity: tech_debt`

## Issue Summary
**Original Spec:** n/a
**Issue:** `copyFragment` was changed to derive `requestedTitle` from `updatedTitle`/`result.title` and `parentPath` from `result.path`, then delegate to `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`. There is no test that stubs `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` on the repository instance and asserts that `copyFragment` calls it with the exact `(requestedTitle, parentPath)` arguments.
**Solution:** Add a `describe('copyFragment', ...)` block in `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` with a single test. The test stubs `aem.sites.cf.fragments.copy` to return a controlled fragment, stubs `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` to reject (halting execution before the untestable `#addToCache`), calls `copyFragment('Updated Title')`, and asserts the stub was called with `('Updated Title', parentPath)` where `parentPath` is derived by dropping the last segment of `result.path`.

## Files to Modify

- `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` — add `describe('copyFragment', ...)` block before `describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle', ...)`

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Insert the new describe block
Insert the following block at line 1526 (between the closing `});` of `describe('deleteFragment', ...)` and the opening of `describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle', ...)`):

```js
    describe('copyFragment', () => {
        it('calls generateUniqueFragmentTitle with requestedTitle derived from updatedTitle and parentPath derived from result.path', async () => {
            const repository = createRepository();
            const copiedFragment = {
                id: 'copied-id',
                path: '/content/dam/mas/sandbox/en_US/cards/cloned-card',
                title: 'Original Title',
                fields: [{ name: 'osi', values: [] }],
            };

            repository.fragmentInEdit = { id: 'source-id' };
            repository.operation = { set: sandbox.stub() };
            repository.search = { value: { path: undefined } };
            repository.processError = sandbox.stub();

            repository.aem = {
                sites: { cf: { fragments: { copy: sandbox.stub().resolves(copiedFragment) } } },
            };

            const generateStub = sandbox
                .stub(repository, 'generateUniqueFragmentTitle')
                .rejects(new Error('stop'));

            await repository.copyFragment('Updated Title');

            const expectedParentPath = '/content/dam/mas/sandbox/en_US/cards';
            expect(generateStub.calledOnce).to.be.true;
            expect(generateStub.firstCall.args[0]).to.equal('Updated Title');
            expect(generateStub.firstCall.args[1]).to.equal(expectedParentPath);
        });

        it('passes result.title as requestedTitle when updatedTitle equals result.title', async () => {
            const repository = createRepository();
            const copiedFragment = {
                id: 'copied-id',
                path: '/content/dam/mas/sandbox/en_US/cards/cloned-card',
                title: 'Same Title',
                fields: [],
            };

            repository.fragmentInEdit = { id: 'source-id' };
            repository.operation = { set: sandbox.stub() };
            repository.search = { value: { path: undefined } };
            repository.processError = sandbox.stub();

            repository.aem = {
                sites: { cf: { fragments: { copy: sandbox.stub().resolves(copiedFragment) } } },
            };

            const generateStub = sandbox
                .stub(repository, 'generateUniqueFragmentTitle')
                .rejects(new Error('stop'));

            await repository.copyFragment('Same Title');

            expect(generateStub.calledOnce).to.be.true;
            expect(generateStub.firstCall.args[0]).to.equal('Same Title');
            expect(generateStub.firstCall.args[1]).to.equal('/content/dam/mas/sandbox/en_US/cards');
        });
    });
```

- Place between line 1525 (`});` closing `deleteFragment`) and line 1527 (`describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle'`)
- No new imports needed — `sandbox`, `createRepository`, `createFragment` are already in scope

### Step 2: Verify syntax
Run `node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` to confirm no parse errors.

## Validation

```bash
node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js
```

```bash
cd studio && npx web-test-runner test/mas-repository.test.js --node-resolve --coverage 2>&1 | grep -E "copyFragment|passed|failed|error"
```

## Patch Scope
**Lines of code to change:** ~45 (insert only, no deletions)
**Risk level:** low
**Testing required:** Run `mas-repository.test.js` and confirm the two new `copyFragment` tests pass alongside all existing tests

